From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:19:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: s5kjn1: Report the crop height, not the width

s5kjn1_get_selection() returns the mode width as the height of the
native/crop rectangle, so userspace (libcamera) sees a square sensor
area. Return the mode height.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
index a707cb74..8e4247a8 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn1.c
@@ -1079,7 +1079,7 @@ static int s5kjn1_get_selection(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 		sel->r.left = 0;
 		sel->r.top = 0;
 		sel->r.width = s5kjn1->mode->width;
-		sel->r.height = s5kjn1->mode->width;
+		sel->r.height = s5kjn1->mode->height;
 		return 0;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
